<title>INDIA: India SEBI to issue norms for FII debt investments.</title>
<headline>India SEBI to issue norms for FII debt investments.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) will issue later on Friday guidelines for investments by foreign institutional investors (FIIs) in Indian corporate debt instruments, a top official said.</p>
<p>SEBI executive director Pratip Kar did not give a time for the release.</p>
<p>The government had earlier this year said it would allow FIIs to invest in debt paper other than government securities.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
